diff --git a/docs/user/usage.md b/docs/user/usage.md
index 9da54a1e..84b2cabd 100644
--- a/docs/user/usage.md
+++ b/docs/user/usage.md
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ Usage aggregates history across Codex, Claude Code, Grok Build, OpenCode, Antigr
 
 Open **Settings → Providers → Usage providers → Add hub**, choose the environment, and enter the hub URL and management key. Pools Codex, Claude, and Grok accounts under **Usage → Limits** (including Codex **Use reset**). Configure the provider's endpoint to the same URL if you want threads to display that hub's limits.
 
+In H3 Code, turn on **Antigravity limits** on a configured hub to add its Antigravity accounts. H3 Code uses the same `H3Code` HTTP user agent from every installation. Shared provider accounts count once when the hub reports the same login. Google may refuse third-party quota requests, in which case the account appears with its latest quota read marked unavailable.
+
 ## Connect an HTTP quota source
 
 Open **Settings → Providers → Usage providers → Add HTTP source** with a GET endpoint (and optional bearer token) returning:
